    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102289" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τάναγρα</span></b> , ἡ, a town of
		Boeotia, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			9.15
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			1.108
		</span></i>, etc. (on the accent, v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.265
		</span></i>):—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ταναγρ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of Tanagra</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.57
			</span></i>, etc.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταναγρ-αῖος</span></b> , ὁ, <i>a man of
				Tanagra</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.4.49
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ταναγραίων φυή</span>,
			prov. of enormous bulk, from a native of T., <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				225
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταναγρ-ίς</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, <i>a woman of T.</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Corinn.
				20
			</span></i> (in poet. dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ταναγρίδεσσι</span>); also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταναγρ-ική</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Sophil.
				4.4
			</span></i>:—ἡ</div>
